        {"unit_id":"u-bba2004f5e2ab75fff2e","start_line":4950,"end_line":4952,"role":"dependency","dependency_reason":"Defines the positive matched-length return reached after '>'."}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "The block parser has a separate type-7 HTML block-start scan when the line is not indented and the container is neither a paragraph nor lazy; a match creates an HTML block. This is a separate route for tag-shaped input, with equivalence to inline HTML tag recognition unestablished by these lines.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id":"u-5aaaeff8fc8ccb21d0cc","start_line":1044,"end_line":1053,"role":"primary","dependency_reason":""}
